## Phase 2: Setup Log Router (Proxmox Host)

We run Vector directly on the Proxmox host. This allows a single service to handle log aggregation for any LXC or Docker container agentlessly.

### 1. Register the Official APT Repository Manually
Run these commands in your Proxmox Host shell:

```bash
# Install dependencies
apt-get update && apt-get install -y apt-transport-https curl gnupg

# Download Datadog's verified public GPG key
curl -sSf https://keys.datadoghq.com/DATADOG_APT_KEY_CURRENT.public | gpg --dearmor | tee /usr/share/keyrings/datadog-archive-keyring.gpg > /dev/null

# Register the stable APT source using the keyring
echo "deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/datadog-archive-keyring.gpg] https://apt.vector.dev/ stable vector-0" | tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/vector.list

# Install Vector
apt-get update
apt-get install -y vector
```

